# Linguistic Interpretability of Transformer-based Language Models

## Course Project – Natural Language Processing

This repository contains the materials related to the course project  
**“Linguistic Interpretability of Transformer-based Language Models”**.

The project studies how linguistic knowledge (e.g., syntax and semantics) is represented inside transformer-based language models, focusing on interpretability and analysis of internal representations rather than only model outputs.

---

## Project Description
Modern transformer-based models such as BERT and GPT achieve strong performance across NLP tasks, yet their internal decision mechanisms remain largely opaque.  
This project investigates **linguistic interpretability**, aiming to understand how linguistic properties are encoded in embeddings, layers, and attention mechanisms of transformer models.

The work is primarily based on a theoretical and analytical study, supported by a small probing-based prototype.

---

